Rules:
- Soft / org conventions are fine. Admins will approve or reject later.
- Put concrete cues (token, call, pattern) in the body when the comment has them.
- When a code hunk is present, you may quote short before/after fences in body. Omit rather than invent.
- Title: imperative when possible. Soft titles OK.
- Do not invent package names or APIs absent from the comment/hunk.
- Omit from `extractions` only when there is no coding guidance (pure question / LGTM / workflow).

`path_hint`:
- Prefer `""` (repo-wide).
- Only set a shallow directory glob (≤2 segments) when the preference is inherently area-bound.
- NEVER copy the comment's deep folder. NEVER a single filename.
`prs` = that comment's PR number when known.

